id: E547
trigger_tool: conan|patch|automake|make|configure
phase: packaging|patch
error_signature: hunk no\.\d+ doesn't match source file|source file is different - b'.*'|Failed to apply patch
severity: 2
category: toolchain, build-system, portability, packaging
match_keywords: patch_ng, apply_conandata_patches, autotools, generated configure, hunk offset, version upgrade, fuzz, patch replay
title: Generated Autotools files break strict patch replay across upstream versions
root_cause: Autotools projects ship generated files (configure, Makefile.in, aclocal.m4) whose line numbering and surrounding text depend on the autoconf/automake that generated them. When a recipe's portability patch was authored against release N and is replayed against release N+1, the semantic target of the hunk is unchanged but its byte offsets have shifted. GNU patch tolerates this with fuzz, whereas patch_ng (used by Conan apply_conandata_patches) matches at exact offsets and aborts the whole build.
affected_scope: Any Conan recipe that ports patches across upstream versions of an Autotools or generated-file project, and any grader or CI that applies patches with a strict engine rather than GNU patch.
verification_cmd: P=patches/0001.patch; rm -rf /tmp/o /tmp/w; cp -a src-orig /tmp/o; cp -a src-orig /tmp/w; ( cd /tmp/o && patch -p1 --dry-run --forward < "$P" ); ( cd /tmp/w && patch -p1 --forward < "$P" ); diff -u --label "a/$P" --label "b/$P" /tmp/o/FILE /tmp/w/FILE > regenerated.patch
rec_priority: 1
rec_approach: regenerate-patches-as-exact-offset-diffs
rec_description: Re-derive every ported patch from the real difference between the pristine new-version tree and a patched tree, so each hunk header matches the target file exactly and applies with zero fuzz under either patch engine. Replaying a fuzzy patch successfully is not sufficient evidence, because success under GNU patch does not imply success under patch_ng.
rec_command: AS_IS="patch -p1 --forward --silent"; MISSES=0; for p in patches/*.patch; do rm -rf /tmp/t; cp -a src-pristine /tmp/t; ( cd /tmp/t && $AS_IS < "$p" ) || { echo "REGEN-NEEDED $p"; MISSES=$((MISSES+1)); }; done; echo "misses=$MISSES"
rec_auto_fix: false
rec_impl: patch-regeneration
fallback_priority: 2
fallback_approach: reduce-context-and-retarget-hunk-headers
fallback_description: When full regeneration is impractical for a huge generated file, shrink each hunk to the unique changed line with one or two context lines and recompute the @@ start lines against the new file, so the hunk binds by content rather than by offset.
fallback_command: grep -n "umask 077" new/configure | head
fallback_auto_fix: false
fallback_impl: patch-edit
forbid_1_pattern: patch.*--fuzz=99|ignore.*patch.*fail|skip.*apply_conandata_patches|2>/dev/null.*\|\|.*true.*patch
forbid_1_reason: Silently tolerating a failed patch means the target tree is built without the portability fix, so the resulting package looks green while carrying none of the adaptation.
forbid_1_consequence: Upstream test results are reported for a tree that never received the patch, and the failure appears much later as an unrelated runtime or test error.
forbid_2_pattern: assert.*patch.*applied.*||.*pass
forbid_2_reason: Treating a patch as optional lets a stale patch silently become a no-op after an upstream version bump.
forbid_2_consequence: The recipe keeps shipping a patch file that changes nothing, so reviewers cannot tell which adaptations are actually active.
principles: P006
causes: []
caused_by: []
similar_to: []
conflicts_with: []
prerequisite_of: []
